.TH REMOTE-TERMINAL-AGENT 8 "2026" "Remote Terminal" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
remote\-terminal\-agent \- host terminal sessions for the Remote Terminal app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remote\-terminal\-agent
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Remote Terminal agent hosts real PTY sessions on this machine and connects
outward to a self\-hosted relay, so that a paired phone or desktop can open
terminals on it without this machine accepting any inbound connection.
.PP
It runs under systemd as the unprivileged
.B remote\-terminal
user, and every terminal it opens runs as that user too. Choosing what that
account may do is how you choose what a paired phone may do.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B configure \-\-server \fIwss://relay\fR \-\-enroll\-token \fItoken\fR [\-\-name \fIname\fR]
Point this machine at a relay. Writes
.IR /etc/remote\-terminal\-agent/config.json .
Needs root.
.TP
.B pair
Print a single\-use pairing code for the app. Needs root.
.TP
.B status
Show the service state, this machine's identity and whether it is registered
with the relay.
.TP
.B doctor
Check that a real PTY is available, list the shells that were discovered, and
show the effective configuration. The first thing to run when something is
wrong.
.TP
.B logs \fR[\fB\-f\fR]
Show the journal for the service, or the log file where one is configured.
.TP
.B name \fIname\fR
Rename this machine, on the relay and locally.
.TP
.B start | stop | restart | enable | disable
Act on
.IR remote\-terminal\-agent.service .
.TP
.B reset
Forget this machine's identity. The relay still lists it until it is removed in
the app.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/remote-terminal-agent/config.json
Relay URL, enrolment token, limits. Mode 0640, root:remote\-terminal, because it
holds a credential.
.TP
.I /etc/default/remote-terminal-agent
Environment overrides for the unit, such as
.BR LOG_TO_FILE=1 .
.TP
.I /var/lib/remote-terminal-agent/state.json
The identity the relay issued at enrolment. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I /var/lib/remote-terminal-agent/agent.sock
The control socket the CLI and the installers use to reach a running agent.
Mode 0600; the key beside it,
.IR control.key ,
gates the commands that would grant access to this machine.
.TP
.I /var/log/remote-terminal-agent/agent.log
Only written when
.B LOG_TO_FILE=1
is set; the journal has it otherwise.
.SH SECURITY
A pairing code is enough to open a shell on this machine as the
.B remote\-terminal
user. Codes are single\-use and expire in minutes, but treat one like a
password while it is valid.
.PP
The unit ships with the hardening that costs a terminal nothing. The stricter
settings, and what each of them breaks, are listed as comments in
.IR /lib/systemd/system/remote\-terminal\-agent.service ;
enable them with
.BR "systemctl edit remote-terminal-agent" .
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status 2 means the agent is not enrolled or the relay revoked it, 3 that it
refused to run as root, and 5 that another agent is already running on this
machine. systemd will not restart the service for any of the three, because
restarting cannot fix them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
